internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00170_f44cfa7e__temp0.10__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00170_f44cfa7e,arc,arc_challenge,arc,170,C,1,"To determine the primary force that must be overcome to keep a heavy box sliding across a carpeted floor at a constant speed, I need to consider the forces acting on the box. The key here is understanding that for an object to move at a constant speed, the net force acting on it must be zero. This means that any force trying to slow it down must be balanced by an equal force in the opposite direction.",C,C,1,90,0,0,78,256,-0.11856953799724579,0.3902776837348938,1.0437482595443726,19.748449325561523,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.46,1.0,75.63644696213305,3.3846116559145742,16.430450916290283,7,0.1,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,489,256,"```json
{
  ""thought"": ""To determine the primary force that must be overcome to keep a heavy box sliding across a carpeted floor at a constant speed, I need to consider the forces acting on the box. The key here is understanding that for an object to move at a constant speed, the net force acting on it must be zero. This means that any force trying to slow it down must be balanced by an equal force in the opposite direction."",
