internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00393_365cb767__temp0.10__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00393_365cb767,arc,arc_challenge,arc,393,C,2,"To maintain the integrity of the experiment and ensure that the results from different groups can be compared fairly, it is essential that all groups adhere to identical conditions. Using the same equipment and procedures is the most critical factor because it minimizes the introduction of external variables that could otherwise lead to inconsistent or biased outcomes. While starting the experiment at the same time and having different members record results can affect the timing and reliability of the data, respectively, they are not as fundamental to the comparability of the results as using the same equipment and procedures.",C,C,1,90,0,0,99,256,-0.19769173860549927,0.5072425603866577,0.9926436543464661,17.138416290283203,5.766558647155762,0.03647977113723755,0.3974358974358974,3.46,0.95,79.0893467636779,3.2368455484268717,16.430450916290283,7,0.1,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,720,256,"```json
