{
  ""thought"": ""When two objects push off each other, they exert equal and opposite forces on each other according to Newton's third law. Since both the man and the boy have the same force applied to them, their accelerations will be inversely proportional to their masses. The man, being heavier, will have a smaller acceleration compared to the boy, who is lighter. Therefore, the boy will move faster, but the man will cover more distance due to his greater mass."",
  ""answer"": ""A"",
  ""confidence"": 90,
  ""stop"": false
}
