internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00007_55ae159f__temp0.60__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00007_55ae159f,arc,arc_challenge,arc,7,A,1,"To determine which geological process formed the Alps, Appalachians, and Himalayas, I need to consider the nature of these mountain ranges. The Alps are known for their folding due to the collision of the African and Eurasian plates. The Appalachians were once part of the supercontinent Pangaea and have been shaped by multiple tectonic movements. The Himalayas are the result of the ongoing collision between the Indian and Eurasian plates. All these ranges are associated with large-scale tectonic activity.",C,C,0,90,0,0,80,256,-0.22042234241962433,0.45734888315200806,0.9077439904212952,16.97730827331543,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.46,0.0,70.41932106018066,3.6353659215376597,16.430450916290283,7,0.6,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,583,256,"{
