internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00256_73563be9__temp0.60__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00256_73563be9,arc,arc_challenge,arc,256,C,1,"To address the decline in Steller sea lion population, it is essential to ensure they have sufficient food. Since herring are crucial for their survival and Pollock feed on herring, increasing the number of Pollock could lead to a decrease in herring availability, which would be counterproductive. Changing the diet of the sea lions might not be feasible as herring are a necessary part of their diet. Moving the sea lions to different locations does not address the underlying food source issue. Therefore, the most logical step is to improve the habitats of herring to ensure there are enough herring available for the sea lions.",C,C,1,85,0,0,105,256,-0.26622024178504944,0.5499428510665894,0.9600846171379089,16.06037139892578,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.41,1.0,50.99656047206372,5.019946396977863,16.430450916290283,7,0.6,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,717,256,"```json
