internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00322_a862010b__temp0.60__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00322_a862010b,arc,arc_challenge,arc,322,C,1,"To determine the most accurate method for measuring how long it takes 2 g of salt to dissolve in 50 mL of water, we need to consider factors like consistency, precision, and the ability to detect minor variations. Option A has only one student taking measurements for one experiment, which might introduce individual error. Option B has two students but still only measures one experiment, which could miss random errors. Option C has one student measuring three identical experiments, which increases consistency but doesn't account for the variability across different experiments. Option D has three students measuring two identical experiments, which maximizes consistency and reduces the impact of individual errors while providing multiple data points for comparison.",D,D,0,90,0,0,118,256,-0.29076382517814636,0.639111340045929,1.1248935461044312,16.25493621826172,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.46,0.0,54.8192652403377,4.669891120897901,16.430450916290283,7,0.6,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,858,256,"```json
{
