internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00340_261864e1__temp0.60__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00340_261864e1,arc,arc_challenge,arc,340,C,2,"Given that the behavior of the helium balloons changes based on the season, it's logical to consider the effect of temperature on gas expansion. Helium, like any gas, expands when heated and contracts when cooled. This principle aligns with the observed practice of inflating balloons less in summer to prevent over-expansion and potential rupture.",C,C,1,85,0,0,56,256,-0.16443473100662231,0.4210144877433777,0.9286948442459106,20.465530395507812,3.662799835205078,0.014068365097045898,0.2222222222222222,3.41,0.95,58.343879834748805,4.387778130715434,16.430450916290283,7,0.6,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,433,256,"```json
{
