internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00071_78c9064f__temp1.00__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00071_78c9064f,arc,arc_challenge,arc,71,D,1,"To determine the effect of different colors of light on plant growth, we must isolate the variable that is manipulated: the color of the light. This means that all other variables should be kept constant to ensure that any observed differences in flower production are due solely to the light color. Therefore, the color of the light bulb should be the only variable that differs across the groups.",D,D,1,100,1,0,68,256,-0.2397109866142273,0.4568207263946533,1.0095654726028442,19.773719787597656,0.0,0.0,0.0,3.56,1.0,29.4583818661049,8.69022613541975,16.430450916290283,7,1.0,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,491,256,"```json
