internlm3_8b_instruct__arc_test_00071_78c9064f__temp1.00__seed7,internlm3_8b_instruct,internlm/InternLM3-8B-Instruct,arc_test_00071_78c9064f,arc,arc_challenge,arc,71,D,2,"If the goal is to isolate the effect of different colors of light on plant growth, it's crucial to maintain uniformity in all other conditions. Any variation in soil type, water amount, or pot color could introduce confounding variables that might affect flower production. Therefore, the correct approach is to use the same type of soil, amount of water, and pots for all groups, ensuring that the only difference is the color of the light bulb. This way, any observed differences in flower production will directly correlate with the color of the light.",D,D,1,100,1,0,94,256,-0.2561306953430176,0.48086413741111755,1.040974736213684,17.382038116455078,5.780755996704102,0.04029148817062378,0.358974358974359,3.56,0.95,33.68461187975481,7.599909445709291,16.430450916290283,7,1.0,cuda,minimal_json,default,0,1,json_exact,json_field,json_field,json_field,1,0,640,256,"```json
