👉 In the forest ecosystem, decomposers like bacteria and fungi are crucial for breaking down leaves into nutrients. The presence of more decomposers means more leaves will be broken down faster, leading to increased nutrient availability in the topsoil. This directly supports the efficient recycling of nutrients. Thus, the most likely change to have a positive impact on the nutrients available in the topsoil is the increase in the number of decomposers."
