In which direction do the roots of plants grow?
A. in the direction of moisture only
B. in the direction of the pull of gravity only
C. in the direction of water and the pull of gravity
D. in the direction of water and away from the pull of gravity



To determine the correct direction of plant root growth, we need to consider two key factors: the availability of water and the effect of gravity. Plants grow towards sources of water and nutrients, which are often found in the soil below them. Additionally, gravity pulls roots downward, assisting them in anchoring themselves and growing deeper into the soil."
